--- body ---
## Context

Three adapters landed on 2026-09-02/03, taking the roster from two seats to
five. Between them they surfaced two defects in `bench/acceptance/assertions.py`
that are the layer's, not any adapter's. Neither was repaired in the batch, and
that was the right call at the time: repairing the layer from inside an adapter
merge request is exactly the coupling the lane spent the night avoiding, and
neither gap changed a single verdict on the roster as it stands.

Neither stays harmless. Gap 1 fires the moment a target emits
`locality == "none"` -- which is narrower than "offers `status`", and the
difference is this ticket's own subject. One such target is already on the
roster with no committed run.

### Gap 1 — a target that honestly reports "no embedder" is scored `fail`

`assertions.py:23` declares the shape as
`"locality": "local" | "remote" | "none"`. `assertions.py:300`, inside
`check_local_by_default`, computes:

    result=PASS if locality == "local" and active is True else FAIL,

Three declared values, a two-way comparison. A target that reports the string
`"none"` is scored **fail against a clause reading "the embedder is local"**.
It is not failing to be local; it has no embedder.

The sharpest form of it is the asymmetry one line above. `assertions.py:294`
returns **not-run** when `locality is None` -- the adapter cannot answer. So a
target that says "I do not know" is scored not-run, while a target that says
"I have no embedder" is scored fail. The honest answer is punished harder than
the ignorant one, which inverts what the layer is for.

Zotero core #6012's shipped default is precisely this case:
`embeddings.model` ships `""` (`build/defaults/preferences/zotero.js:120-125`
at the pinned commit) and `isEnabled()` returns false
(`xpcom/embeddings.js:179-181`).

### Gap 2 — three of the seven ratified verbs are the subject of no assertion

The ratified interface is `install`, `uninstall`, `configure`, `query`,
`status`, `pause`, `resume`. The five checks registered in `assertions.py`'s
`ALL` carry four distinct verbs between them as their subject: `status`
(`R10-local-by-default`), `query` (`R10-no-egress`), `install`
(`R15-residue-inventory`), `query` (`R15-model-cache-under-declared-roots`),
`uninstall` (`R15-uninstall-removes-declared-state`).

So `configure`, `pause` and `resume` can yield no check state at all, however
a target is written. `pause` is the decisive one: it occurs **zero times** in
the whole of `assertions.py`, so no reading of the file rescues it.

Be careful with the wording, because a loose version of this was written and
corrected during the batch: `configure` and `resume` ARE named in
`assertions.py` -- in `EGRESS_VERBS` and in `check_local_by_default`'s
precondition loop -- and a target not offering `configure` gets a
`not-offered` Check carrying `verb="configure"`. What is true is that only
four verbs are ever a check's **subject**, and that `pause` is named nowhere.

The consequence is a ticket-level one: every adapter ticket carries the exit
criterion "every interface verb yields pass, fail, not-offered or not-run",
and that criterion is **unsatisfiable by any adapter under the current
layer**. 0584 closed with the reading recorded; 0583 closed with the same
criterion ticked bare. Either the layer grows assertions naming the missing
verbs, or the criterion is reworded to what it can mean.

## Relevant files

- `bench/acceptance/assertions.py` -- both gaps; `:23`, `:294`, `:300` for
  gap 1, the `ALL` registry at `:548` for gap 2
- `bench/acceptance/interface.py` -- the ratified seven-verb interface; owned
  by `SPEC.md` §5.2.8 and the `DECISIONS.md` entry ratified 2026-09-02
- `tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zotero_core_6012.py:498,520` -- gap 1 already
  driven red with a discriminating control arm; do not rewrite these, make
  them the regression test
- `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py:237` -- **the target that makes gap 1
  live.** It declares only `uninstall` and `resume` absent, emits the
  normalized shape, and maps a falsy `effective` straight onto the string
  `"none"`: `{"local": "local"}.get(effective, "remote" if effective else
  "none")`. That is the exact FAIL input. Its own docstring records that
  without a model-runtime path the target falls back to keyword-only
  silently, so `effective` goes falsy and the row flips to `fail` on a
  machine that is merely unprovisioned
- `bench/acceptance/adapters/zotero_mcp.py:572-596` -- the OTHER half of the
  same asymmetry, and not the live one. It offers `status` and reaches
  `check_local_by_default`, but its `status()` returns no `"embedding"` key
  at all, so `locality` is `None` and the check takes the not-run branch at
  `:294`. It sits on the ignorant side: it says "I do not know", not "I have
  no embedder"
- `tickets/closed/0583-...erg`, `tickets/closed/0584-...erg` -- where both
  findings currently rest

## Actions

1. Rule on gap 1's remedy before coding it. The obvious repair -- score
   `"none"` as `not-offered` or as its own state -- is a change to what a
   ratified clause MEANS, not a bug fix, so it may be the author's call
   rather than the lane's. State the options and their costs in the ticket
   before editing.
2. Apply the chosen remedy in `assertions.py`, touching nothing else.
3. Rule on gap 2: grow the layer with assertions whose subject is
   `configure`, `pause` or `resume`, or reword the adapter-ticket exit
   criterion. These are different amounts of work and the second is not a
   climb-down -- an interface verb that no requirement constrains may
   legitimately have no assertion.
4. Whichever way gap 2 goes, leave a pointer where the next assertion author
   will meet it: a comment in `assertions.py` beside `ALL`, not only a
   ticket.

## Test

Red first, and gap 1's red already exists:
`test_a_target_with_no_embedder_is_scored_fail_by_the_local_by_default_clause`
drives a fake reporting `"none"` through the real `check_local_by_default` and
asserts FAIL, carrying the message "if this passes, the layer has been changed
and this finding is stale". Its control arm asserts `("local") == PASS` and
`("remote") == FAIL`. Both are green today. The remedy inverts the first, and
the control must stay green -- if both move, the fix is too wide.

For gap 2, the test is a registry-coverage assertion: for each of the seven
ratified verbs, either some registered check names it as its subject, or the
verb appears in an explicit, argued exemption list. A bare count would pass
against a wrong-shaped registry.

## Verification

- [ ] `check_local_by_default` on a target reporting `"none"` yields the
      ruled-on state, and the `"local"`/`"remote"` control arm is unmoved
- [ ] `zoteus`, whose `status()` can emit `"none"`, produces a defensible
      `R10-local-by-default` row -- this is the target that makes gap 1 live,
      and `zotero-mcp` is the control beside it, since its row must stay
      not-run for the different, correct reason
- [ ] the seven-verb coverage test fails against today's `ALL` before it passes
- [ ] `make check` and `erg check tickets/` pass

## Invariants

- The layer names no target. `tests/test_acceptance_layer_is_target_neutral.py`
  must stay green; do not fix gap 1 by special-casing a target.
- No committed verdict is silently revised. If a remedy changes what an
  existing artifact's row should read, regenerate the artifact from the edited
  code and say so -- an artifact whose provenance is "the code before the last
  edit" is the defect this repo keeps paying for.
- `RATIFIED_TARGETS`'s comment in the neutrality test still reads "Four have
  no adapter yet"; that was true when written and is now stale, all five
  having adapters. Correct it if you are in the file; it is not this ticket's
  subject.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] gap 1 ruled on and applied, with the control arm demonstrably unmoved
- [ ] gap 2 ruled on: either the layer covers the missing verbs, or the
      adapter-ticket exit criterion is reworded to what it can mean
- [ ] a pointer to whichever gap remains open sits in `assertions.py`, not
      only in a closed ticket
- [ ] `make check` and `erg check tickets/` pass
